// spec: LEX-018
//
// ⚠️ A defect is a statement about the INTERPRETER and is never compiled.
//
// ⚠️ THE LITERAL HALF IS FIXED.  A literal outside the range is refused where
// it is read -- refusals/0035 -- so a value the source states plainly is no
// longer silently replaced by a different one.
//
// What remains is ARITHMETIC.  LEX-018 requires a result outside the range to
// raise; it wraps, so this prints -2147483648 rather than failing.  That half
// touches every operator and is the one place in this generation where the
// cost is per-operation rather than per-declaration.

WriteLn (2147483647 + 1);
